{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>His own hands shall bring, etc.</b> The hands of the owners should be on top, and the fat and the breast placed in them, and the hand of the priest underneath, and he waves them (Menachot 61)." "<b>The fire-offerings of YHWH.</b> And what are the fire-offerings?" "<b>He shall bring the fat upon the breast.</b> When he brings it from the slaughter area, he places the fat on the breast, and when he gives it to the priest who waves, the breast is found on top and the fat below. And this is what is said in another place: ״the thigh of heave-offering and the breast of wave-offering upon the fire-offerings of the fat they shall bring to wave, etc.״ (Leviticus 10). And after the waving he gives it to the priest who burns it, and the breast is found below. And this is what is said: ״and they placed the fats upon the breasts and he burned the fats on the altar״ (ibid. 9). We learn that three priests are required for it — so it is explained in Menachot." "<b>He shall bring the fat upon the breast.</b> And why does he bring the breast? To wave it — that is why he brings it, not that it should be among the fire-offerings. For since it says <b>the fire-offerings of YHWH — the fat upon the breast</b>, one might think the breast too is for the fire-offerings; therefore it says <b>the breast to wave, etc.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:26.701058743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}